*> PLB-Q013 select-into-no-where: a singleton SELECT with no WHERE.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. SELALL.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
    EXEC SQL INCLUDE SQLCA END-EXEC.
01  WS-NAME             PIC X(30).
01  WS-COUNT            PIC S9(9) COMP.
01  WS-DATE             PIC X(10).
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    *> Reported: every row, and a row for each group.
    EXEC SQL SELECT NAME INTO :WS-NAME FROM CUSTOMER END-EXEC
    EXEC SQL SELECT REGION, COUNT(*) INTO :WS-NAME, :WS-COUNT
             FROM CUSTOMER GROUP BY REGION END-EXEC
    *> Not reported: a WHERE (not one in a subquery alone), aggregates
    *> only, a one-row table, and FETCH FIRST ROW ONLY.
    EXEC SQL SELECT NAME INTO :WS-NAME FROM CUSTOMER
             WHERE ID IN (SELECT ID FROM VIP) END-EXEC
    EXEC SQL SELECT MAX(ID), COUNT(*) INTO :WS-COUNT, :WS-COUNT
             FROM CUSTOMER END-EXEC
    EXEC SQL SELECT CURRENT DATE INTO :WS-DATE
             FROM SYSIBM.SYSDUMMY1 END-EXEC
    EXEC SQL SELECT NAME INTO :WS-NAME FROM CUSTOMER
             FETCH FIRST 1 ROW ONLY END-EXEC
    IF SQLCODE NOT = 0
        DISPLAY SQLCODE
    END-IF
    GOBACK.
